\cf2 The text itself is remarkably sparse. It asks about vine wood's utility, establishes its worthlessness for any purpose except burning, and applies this to Jerusalem's inhabitants. The "you will know" addressed to the audience and the reference to some who "came out of fire" are intriguing but not explicitly explained within this chapter.\
