Marshwiggle: The text, at least, makes a grammatical distinction between the two groups of exiles in verse 7. Them, versus you. Chapter 14 explicitly opens with elders coming physically to Ezekiel and being answered, and chapter 1 tells us that Ezekiel is already in exile in Babylon.\
But what to do with this distinction will need careful attention to the text. Pulling in the chapters written before chapter 15, or parts of the Bible Ezekiel was drawing on, is acceptable evidence for what the text is doing though.\
Opus: You're right to call for more careful attention. Let me work with what's grammatically clear in verse 7:\
