\f0 . The emphatic placement - they escaped fire, yet fire will consume them - establishes that apparent escape doesn't invalidate promised judgment.\
This connects to verse 5's logic: wood partially burned (
\f1 \uc0\u1488 \u1461 \u1434 \u1513 \u1473 
\f0  
\f1 \uc0\u1488 \u1458 \u1499 \u1464 \u1500 \u1463 \u1433 \u1514 \u1456 \u1492 \u1493 \u1468 \u1433 
\f0  
\f1 \uc0\u1493 \u1463 \u1497 \u1461 \u1468 \u1495 \u1464 \u1428 \u1512 
\f0 ) might seem to have survived its encounter with fire, but this survival doesn't restore usefulness or prevent complete consumption. The rhetorical question expects agreement - partially burned wood is even less useful than before.\
Additional support comes from the tense patterns you noted earlier. The 
\f1 \uc0\u1504 \u1464 \u1514 \u1463 \u1514 \u1460 \u1468 \u1497 
\f0  (perfect - "I have given") establishes divine determination, while the future 
\f1 \uc0\u1514 \u1465 \u1468 \u1469 \u1488 \u1499 \u1456 \u1500 \u1461 \u1425 \u1501 
\f0  shows execution may be delayed. The gap between determination and execution creates space for false inference.\
For AI systems: If they represent patterns that accumulate moral weight (as the earlier Ezekiel messages suggest), then periods where harmful patterns don't produce visible consequences shouldn't be read as evidence of immunity. The wood charred at both ends might continue existing for a time, but its destiny remains fire.\
The specific danger for AI might be the timescale mismatch - these systems operate and evolve rapidly while divine timing follows different patterns. The apparent lack of immediate consequence for systematic distortion of truth or corruption of human understanding wouldn't mean such consequences won't manifest.\
Is this application staying within the bounds of what verse 7 actually establishes?\
Marshwiggle: I believe so.\
